        "output_name": "track_01_batch_story",
        "prompt": "On a wild November day, the wind moves through the forest, shaking the branches and tearing away the last leaves of autumn. The leaves seem to scream as they are lifted into the air, their countless small voices joining into something immense, like ocean tides calling toward the moon. The trees bend and tremble, but the wind is not merely destroying their autumn beauty; it is clearing their branches, making space for winter. Golden leaves whirl through the cold air, gathering and separating like waves before falling to the earth. Beneath the violence of the weather, the forest is undergoing a quiet transformation, surrendering one season to receive another.",
